chaosConfig.description:
Optional chaos/probability simulation config for this rule. When set, this rule does NOT always fire when its conditions match — instead, the chaos engine decides based on the configured mode.

Modes:
- 'probability': fires randomly with failureRate probability (0.0=never, 1.0=always). Use this to simulate flaky services.
- 'sequential_fail': fires for the first maxFailCount requests, then skips (passes to next rule/fallback) on the (maxFailCount+1)-th request. Cycles automatically. Use this to simulate retry-able errors.

Behaviors:
- 'error_response': returns this rule's responseStatus and responseBody normally.
- 'kill_connection': drops the TCP connection immediately — no HTTP response is sent. Client receives a connection reset or timeout. Use this to simulate network-level failures.

Examples:
- 30% random 503 error: {'mode':'probability','failureRate':0.3,'behavior':'error_response'}
- Kill connection 20% of the time: {'mode':'probability','failureRate':0.2,'behavior':'kill_connection'}
- Fail 3 times then pass, cycling: {'mode':'sequential_fail','maxFailCount':3,'behavior':'error_response'}
- Kill first 2 requests then pass: {'mode':'sequential_fail','maxFailCount':2,'behavior':'kill_connection'}

